+### Enable Log channels
+You can enable logging for specific log channels by running the following command before launching Safari or other applications:
+```bash
+for identifier in com.apple.WebKit.WebContent.Development com.apple.WebKit.WebContent org.webkit.MiniBrowser -g /Users/$USER/Library/Containers/com.apple.Safari/Data/Library/Preferences/com.apple.Safari.plist; do
+    for key in WebCoreLogging WebKitLogging WebKit2Logging; do
+        defaults write ${identifier} "${key}" "<ChannelName>"
+    done
+done
+```
+You can remove all channels by replacing `<ChannelName>` with an empty string `""`.
+
+Available channels:
+- ITPCustomLog: General custom logging for ITP related features
+- ITPResourceLoading: Resource loading related logging for ITP
+- ITPClassification: Classification related logging for ITP
+- ITPCookieLogs: Cookie related logging for ITPs
+
+You can view the logs in Console.app or by running the following command in Terminal:
+```bash
+log stream --predicate 'category == "<ChannelName1>" OR category == "<ChannelName2>"' --level debug
+```
+
